{
 "_comment": "Written explanations (docs/EXPLANATIONS-PLAN.md): which structures get them and the limits they must meet. Organs are listed here by hand; bones, muscles, vessels, nerves and brain regions are chosen by step 15's rule (the structure's name, its name without left/right, or its numbered class is a key term of the pinned OpenStax A&P 2e), minus the generic terms in `exclude`; cell types are the 70 with morphology profiles; organelles are every organelle a cell model draws. `tiers`: 1 Plain, 2 Core. An organ whose Plain is one of the nine Human Atlas texts gets Core only. `appliesTo`: structures that share the text (left and right, numbered), for a class with no node of its own; step 15 adds left and right instances of a class that is a node. `humanAtlas`: the nine original texts, pinned by checksum (step 12 fails if one changes). `cellGroups`: the tissue groups of the profiled cell types (docs/CELLS-PLAN.md); organs and cell types are drafted three at a time within one system or tissue group, and each of their texts is checked by its own agent.",
